  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "lapsed_date": "13/08/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:115%&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of the under-provision of off-street car parking spaces, absence of information submitted to demonstrate safe access and egress of the proposed off-street vehicle car parking spaces to the site, in conjunction with the proposed siting of the bin stores and soft landscaping to the application site’s frontage, would result in adverse impact on highway safety in terms of occupiers’ and visitors’ unimpeded pedestrian access to the application site and highway safety of wider pedestrian users of the footpath along Whitchurch Lane. The under-provision of sufficient waste bins would fail to provide satisfactory living conditions for future occupiers and would result in disturbance to surrounding neighbouring properties. The proposed development is contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3, D6 and Policies SI7, T6.1 and T4(f) of the London Plan (2021) and Policies GR1, HO2(f), M1, M2 and CE1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:115%&quot;&gt;The vertical stacking of the proposed accommodation is such that the kitchen of Flat 4 would be positioned above the bedroom of ground floor Flat 1, resulting in potential for transfer of noise to a principal habitable room. The application is not supported by an independent Noise Assessment to otherwise demonstrate how noise transference would be mitigated between the proposed ground floor 1-bed self-contained flat (Flat 1) and the proposed first and second floor 1 bedroom flat (Flat 4). This is contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3, D6 and D14 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy GR1.C, Policy HO2.2(d) of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041) and Paragraph 4.55 of Harrow Council&#x27;s adopted Residential Design Guide SPD (2010).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:115%&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of its siting in a Public Transport Accessibility Level (PTAL) rating of 2, and failure to provide family sized housing on the ground floor (where it is possible to do so on the site as demonstrated in the previous planning permission (reference P/3905/22)), would result in over-intensive development in a location with poor accessibility to means of public transport, with poor layout and poor usability and indirect means of access to rear garden space for future residents of the 3-bed family unit, contrary to Policy HO2.1 (b) and (c) and Policy HO2.4 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
